  --- EN description ---
The Van Gogh Museum in Amsterdam is home to the iconic painting The Starry Night, a masterpiece of swirling skies and vibrant colors that captures the emotional depth and innovation of Vincent van Gogh's work. This Amsterdam art museum offers an extensive collection of 197 paintings available online, showcasing the breadth of Van Gogh's artistic journey. In addition to Van Gogh, the collection features works by other notable artists such as Paul Gauguin and Henri de Toulouse-Lautrec, providing a broader context to the Post-Impressionist era.

What sets the Van Gogh Museum apart is its singular focus on the life and works of Vincent van Gogh, making it the largest collection dedicated to a single artist in the world. The museum's building itself, designed by Gerrit Rietveld and later expanded by Kisho Kurokawa, reflects a modern approach to exhibiting art, with spaces that enhance the viewing experience of Van Gogh's masterpieces. This specialized focus allows visitors to gain a deeper understanding of Van Gogh's artistic development and personal struggles.

Art enthusiasts, history buffs, and those curious about Van Gogh's influence on modern art will find this collection particularly enlightening. Explore the 197 works online to discover the depth and passion of Van Gogh's paintings and the era that shaped them.

