  --- EN description ---
One of the most iconic paintings at the Victoria and Albert Museum is J.M.W. Turner's The Fighting Temeraire, celebrated for its romantic depiction of the old warship being towed to its final berth in 1838. This London art museum offers a collection of 87 works available online, showcasing a diverse range of artistic expressions. Alongside Turner, the collection includes works by renowned artists such as John Constable and William Morris, each contributing to the rich tapestry of British art.

What sets the Victoria and Albert Museum apart is its dedication to the decorative arts and design, making it a unique institution in the world of art museums. Founded in 1852, the museum's focus extends beyond traditional paintings to include a wide array of art forms, reflecting the evolution of design and craftsmanship through the ages. Housed in a stunning Victorian building, the museum itself is an architectural masterpiece, adding another layer of historical significance to its offerings.

Art enthusiasts, design students, and history buffs alike will find the Victoria and Albert Museum's collection intriguing for its emphasis on the intersection of art and design. Explore the 87 masterpieces available online to gain insight into the creative minds that shaped the visual culture of their time.

