At the Whitney Museum of American Art, one of the most iconic paintings is Edward Hopper's Early Sunday Morning, a masterful depiction of urban life in 1930s America. This New York art museum offers an extensive collection of 159 works available online, showcasing a wide array of American creativity. In addition to Hopper, the collection features masterpieces by renowned artists such as Georgia O'Keeffe and Alexander Calder, each contributing to the rich tapestry of American art history.

What sets the Whitney Museum apart is its unwavering focus on 20th and 21st-century American art, highlighting both established and emerging artists. Founded in 1930 by Gertrude Vanderbilt Whitney, the museum has been a pioneering force in supporting living artists and presenting innovative exhibitions. Its unique architectural design, created by Renzo Piano, provides a dynamic space that enhances the viewing experience, making it a standout among New York art museums.

Art enthusiasts and history buffs alike will find the Whitney Museum's collection a compelling exploration of American culture and artistic expression. Discover the captivating stories behind each painting and immerse yourself in the evolution of American art by browsing the 159 works available online.

